{"bill_id": 1721, "short_title": "City of London Corporation (Open Spaces) Act 2018", "former_short_title": null, "current_house": "Unassigned", "originating_house": "Commons", "last_update": "2018-03-29T14:54:36", "bill_withdrawn": null, "is_defeated": false, "bill_type_id": 6, "introduced_session_id": 28, "included_session_ids": [28, 29, 30], "is_act": true, "current_stage": {"id": 10344, "stage_id": 11, "session_id": 30, "description": "Royal Assent", "abbreviation": "RA", "house": "Unassigned", "stage_sittings": [{"id": 9460, "stage_id": 11, "bill_stage_id": 10344, "bill_id": 1721, "date": "2018-03-15T00:00:00"}], "sort_order": 17}, "long_title": "To make provision relating to the public open spaces under the management and control of the City of London Corporation; and for related purposes.", "summary": null, "sponsors": [], "promoters": [], "petitioning_period": "The House of Commons petitioning period ended at 5pm on 15 February 2016.
The House of Lords petitioning period ended on 23 October 2017

The deadline for petitioning in the House of Lords is 5pm on 23 October 2017.", "petition_information": "<p>If you are &quot;specially and directly affected&quot; by this Bill you may oppose the Bill or seek its amendment before a Select Committee in either or both Houses.  If you present a &quot;petition&quot; against the bill at the appropriate times (during a &quot;petitioning period&quot;) you may be able to have your views on the bill heard by the Committee (in whichever House you petition). </p><p>There are specific times when petitions can be presented.  <strong>The deadline for petitions  to the House of Commons was 5pm on 15 February 2016</strong>.  <strong>The deadline for petitions to the House of Lords was 5pm on 23 October 2017.  There will be no further opportunities to petition against this Bill.</strong>  </p><p><a>Further information about petitioning</a> can be found by following the link or you can <a>contact </a>one of the Private Bill Offices.  Staff in either office will be happy to answer any questions you may have about the process of opposing a private bill.  </p>", "agent": {"name": "Winckworth Sherwood LLP", "address": "Minerva House, 5 Montagu Close, London, SE1 9BB", "phone_no": "020 7593 5005", "email": "agorlov@wslaw.co.uk", "website": ""}, "detail_ok": 1, "short_title_md5": "61363f084450e79b88f1811383015077", "duplicated": 0}

